From e337727f6dd5a48403c99ab5b8cd7cc9b90ce4a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 01:44:33 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] qualcommax: ipq50xx: ax3000t-v2: let the NAND ECC follow the
 chip

The board forced 4-bit ECC on its SPI-NAND. The stock bootloader does
not use one strength for every unit: it looks the chip up in its own
serial-NAND table and runs 8-bit ECC on the parts with a 128-byte spare
area, 4-bit on those with 64 bytes. In the table of the stock U-Boot on
this board (13 parts), the four 8-bit parts (GigaDevice c8 c1, c8 41,
c8 81, Micron 2c 15) are exactly the ones with 128 bytes of spare.

A unit built with one of those parts has its whole flash written with
8-bit codewords, from SBL1 to ART and the U-Boot environment. With the
forced 4-bit setting, every written page there reads back as an
uncorrectable ECC error and wrong data: 532-byte codewords are decoded
as 528-byte ones, so each page goes wrong at offsets 516-519,
1032-1039 and 1548-1559. One unit in the field shows exactly this on
every partition in the RAM installer, while it boots stock normally. An
image installed there would be written in a layout its own loader cannot
read.

Without the two properties, spi-qpic-snand picks the strength from the
OOB size (0422): 4-bit below 80 bytes, 8-bit from 80, which is the
bootloader's rule for every part both know. The Linux tables give each
of them the spare size the bootloader table gives. On the 64-byte parts
(the ESMT F50D1G41LB most units carry) the result is the same 4-bit,
512-byte-step configuration as before.

Link: https://github.com/ADCDS/xiaomi-openwrt-install/issues/7
---
 target/linux/qualcommax/dts/ipq5018-mi-router-ax3000t-v2.dts | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/target/linux/qualcommax/dts/ipq5018-mi-router-ax3000t-v2.dts b/target/linux/qualcommax/dts/ipq5018-mi-router-ax3000t-v2.dts
index 2a77d95efd..f4d06b2182 100644
--- a/target/linux/qualcommax/dts/ipq5018-mi-router-ax3000t-v2.dts
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommax/dts/ipq5018-mi-router-ax3000t-v2.dts
@@ -156,8 +156,6 @@
 		reg = <0>;
 
 		nand-ecc-engine = <&qpic_nand>;
-		nand-ecc-step-size = <512>;
-		nand-ecc-strength = <4>;
 		nand-bus-width = <8>;
 
 		partitions {
-- 
2.47.3

